    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0008",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "The [`projectionDirection`](scncamera/projectiondirection.md) property determines whether this [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md) property measures the camera’s vertical or horizontal viewing angle, and SceneKit automatically calculates the viewing angle in the other direction to match the aspect ratio of the view displaying the scene.",
      "normalizedSource": "The [`projectionDirection`](scncamera/projectiondirection.md) property determines whether this [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md) property measures the camera’s vertical or horizontal viewing angle, and SceneKit automatically calculates the viewing angle in the other direction to match the aspect ratio of the view displaying the scene.",
      "sourceHash": "1c7ab999a4639eda47cc25babeb7d1324b87dd0b0828197458d860642b302b11",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Discussion",
      "contextAfter": "For example, a [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md) of `60` and the default [`SCNCameraProjectionDirection.vertical`](scncameraprojectiondirection/vertical.md) projection, presented fullscreen on a 16:9 display in portrait orientation, results in a vertical viewing angle of 60° and a horizontal viewing angle of 33.75°.",
      "documentTitle": "fieldOfView",
      "framework": "SceneKit",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0002",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0008",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "For example, a [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md) of `60` and the default [`SCNCameraProjectionDirection.vertical`](scncameraprojectiondirection/vertical.md) projection, presented fullscreen on a 16:9 display in portrait orientation, results in a vertical viewing angle of 60° and a horizontal viewing angle of 33.75°.",
      "normalizedSource": "For example, a [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md) of `60` and the default [`SCNCameraProjectionDirection.vertical`](scncameraprojectiondirection/vertical.md) projection, presented fullscreen on a 16:9 display in portrait orientation, results in a vertical viewing angle of 60° and a horizontal viewing angle of 33.75°.",
      "sourceHash": "d5e48b07acf5b6f48b2f7cee0e60df55695bbbb4652b547d8b77f02552072138",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "The [`projectionDirection`](scncamera/projectiondirection.md) property determines whether this [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md) property measures the camera’s vertical or horizontal viewing angle, and SceneKit automatically calculates the viewing angle in the other direction to match the aspect ratio of the view displaying the scene.",
      "contextAfter": "You can choose to specify viewing angle either directly, using this [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md) property, or in terms that model a physical camera, using the [`sensorHeight`](scncamera/sensorheight.md) and [`focalLength`](scncamera/focallength.md) properties.",
      "documentTitle": "fieldOfView",
      "framework": "SceneKit",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0009:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0009",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "You can choose to specify viewing angle either directly, using this [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md) property, or in terms that model a physical camera, using the [`sensorHeight`](scncamera/sensorheight.md) and [`focalLength`](scncamera/focallength.md) properties.",
      "normalizedSource": "You can choose to specify viewing angle either directly, using this [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md) property, or in terms that model a physical camera, using the [`sensorHeight`](scncamera/sensorheight.md) and [`focalLength`](scncamera/focallength.md) properties.",
      "sourceHash": "39d6015ca4a19c7d6d8d6545b9376a7470f4a40f60644add83571a3ddc85ff35",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "For example, a [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md) of `60` and the default [`SCNCameraProjectionDirection.vertical`](scncameraprojectiondirection/vertical.md) projection, presented fullscreen on a 16:9 display in portrait orientation, results in a vertical viewing angle of 60° and a horizontal viewing angle of 33.75°.",
      "contextAfter": "Setting the [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md) property causes SceneKit to automatically recalculate the [`focalLength`](scncamera/focallength.md) value, and setting the [`sensorHeight`](scncamera/sensorheight.md) or [`focalLength`](scncamera/focallength.md) property recalculates [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md).",
      "documentTitle": "fieldOfView",
      "framework": "SceneKit",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0009:0002",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0009",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "Setting the [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md) property causes SceneKit to automatically recalculate the [`focalLength`](scncamera/focallength.md) value, and setting the [`sensorHeight`](scncamera/sensorheight.md) or [`focalLength`](scncamera/focallength.md) property recalculates [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md).",
      "normalizedSource": "Setting the [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md) property causes SceneKit to automatically recalculate the [`focalLength`](scncamera/focallength.md) value, and setting the [`sensorHeight`](scncamera/sensorheight.md) or [`focalLength`](scncamera/focallength.md) property recalculates [`fieldOfView`](scncamera/fieldofview.md).",
      "sourceHash": "dc9f004ca65fc4e4e29d793bbbcfb27a1d07b70073ce43d91ccf873d7a939dd0",
